<title>LATVIA: LATVIA-UNIBANKA INTRODUCES CASH ACCOUNT.</title>
<headline>LATVIA-UNIBANKA INTRODUCES CASH ACCOUNT.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unibanka, second largest Latvian bank, said on Friday it has introduced a non-interest bearing cash account starting this month.</p>
<p>&quot;If you do not want to keep foreign exchange at home, leave it in the bank and pay in or withdraw at any time,&quot; the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>The opening of the account costs 1.50 lats for an individual and 10 lats for a legal entity. It is free for Unibanka clients who already have payment accounts.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
